Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.80,0:00:07.00,Default,,0,0,0,,When an LLM voice agent takes a call, mid-sentence caller barge-ins and unsanitized stage tags break conversation state.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.10,0:00:13.68,Default,,0,0,0,,TurnProof solves this for AssemblyAI Text-to-Speech.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.50,0:00:19.20,Accent,,0,0,0,,[Voice Agent Audio · 4,620ms]: "Thanks for calling Alliance Appliance Repair. Your booking code is 4-9-3-A..." [Barge-In Cut]
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.50,0:00:28.80,Default,,0,0,0,,The acoustic waveform scissor slices the turn at the exact caller interruption millisecond, so unreached words never pollute agent memory.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.80,0:00:34.00,Defect,,0,0,0,,[Defect Audio]: "Pause. Thanks for calling..." (Vocalizing stage tag [pause])
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.00,0:00:46.80,Default,,0,0,0,,In Studio, the pre-flight compiler catches vocalized tags like bracket pause before billing a character, and formats alphanumeric codes for clean spoken cadence.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.50,0:00:57.30,Default,,0,0,0,,At the interrupt cut-point, unreached entities like prescription codes and prices are tagged as withheld, and patched directly into the LLM conversation state.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.50,0:01:12.50,Default,,0,0,0,,In Verify, TurnProof wraps synthesized PCM audio into a container and transcribes it back through Universal-3.5 Pro to verify that every entity survives synthesis.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.50,0:01:23.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Sanitized turns achieve a one hundred percent entity lock, while unsanitized drafts fail due to vocalized stage tags transcribed in the readback.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.00,0:01:35.10,Default,,0,0,0,,In Ledger, inspect reproducible bug-bounty telemetry with live request IDs, and copy production TypeScript or Python barge-in handlers.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.00,0:01:41.20,Accent,,0,0,0,,TurnProof: acoustic precision for production voice agents on AssemblyAI.
